# prerelease — no pre-release builds are promoted, so these land on stable
# downloads rather than /next, which renders only "Pre-release downloads are
# currently unavailable". Pointed straight at /download rather than at /next
# so none of them chain through a second redirect.
#
# 302, deliberately, NOT 301. This is temporary — it holds only while there's
# no active alpha/beta. A 301 tells browsers and search engines the move is
# permanent: browsers cache it indefinitely (users who hit /beta once would
# keep being sent to /download long after we restore the page, with no way for
# us to clear their cache), and search engines drop the old URL and move its
# ranking signals to the target. A 302 leaves /next as the known URL and is
# undone the moment this rule is removed.
#
# To promote a pre-release again: restore /alpha, /beta and /next to point at
# the pre-release downloads, and set isActive on the entry in
# src/assets/data/audacityReleases.ts. Then drop the sitemap filter for /next
# in astro.config.mjs.
/alpha	/download	302
/beta	/download	302

# /next was the Audacity 4 pre-release page; for launch it lands on the
# Audacity 4 promo. Note /nightly chains through here.
/next	/audacity-4	302

# /au4 was the pre-release shortlink, then a page of its own; the Audacity 4
# promo now lives at /audacity-4, so it lands there. 302 while the launch-day
# route could still change.
/au4	/audacity-4	302

